  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.1. Increased capacity of Member States to ensure respect for, promote and realize fundamental principles and rights at work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa Bureau of Statistics included modules on Child Labour in the 2023 Labour Force Survey.
In addition, constituents have identified national priorities for the progress of Samoa towards the 2025 Agenda as an 8.7 Alliance Pathfinder country. In 2022 the ILO worked with the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Labour to conduct awareness workshops on Child Labour and held a National Consultation on the Rapid Assessment successfully finalising and launching the report. Technical support was also provided to the Samoa Bureau of Statistics to include modules on Child Labour in the 2023 Labour Force Survey. Technical support to the tripartite stakeholders was provided for a national workshop to map out the national priorities for the progress of Samoa towards the 2025 Agenda as an 8.7 Alliance Pathfinder country.  
The ILO provided technical support for the review of the Rapid Assessment on Child Labour conducted by the National University of Samoa as a follow-up to the 2017 report on Child Labour in Samoa and the validation workshop. Ongoing support has also been provided to the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Labour as well as tripartite stakeholders for the formulation of Samoa&#x2019;s National Action Plan on Child Labour as an 8.7 Alliance Pathfinder Country.</narrative>
   </description>
